1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,200
One menu bar app
with many small tools.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,900
Switch on only the ones you want.

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:09,600
Open the widget window:
each gadget is a widget.

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:12,300
Each one switches on or off alone.

5
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:16,400
Click a widget: its settings panel
slides in on the right.

6
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:19,900
Settings, shortcuts and permissions

7
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:23,800
No permission is asked until
you switch a gadget on.

8
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:28,200
Window Snap: 24 keyboard commands,
or drag a window to an edge.

9
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:33,000
System Monitor: CPU, memory, disk,
network and more in the menu bar.

10
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:37,300
Capture Float keeps a capture
floating over other windows.

11
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:41,400
File Shelf: shake while dragging
and a floating shelf appears.

12
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:45,200
Focus Dim darkens everything
behind the window you use.

13
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:49,800
Disk Map shows what fills a disk,
as a sunburst or as blocks.

14
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:56,200
Order a combo: a few gadgets switch
on together for the way you work.

15
00:00:56,700 --> 00:01:01,700
The menu bar quick panel lists every
tool, its status and its controls.

16
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:06,600
Nacho Pet is the Nacho character
in the corner of your screen.

17
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:10,700
Free and open source (MIT)
for macOS 12 or later.

18
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,600
Get it from GitHub Releases.
